1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,400
So today I want to talk about running

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:06,000
language models on your own laptop.

3
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:08,600
A year ago, this would have sounded crazy.

4
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,200
You needed a data center,
or at least

5
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:13,800
a very expensive graphics card.

6
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,400
But the models got smaller,

7
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:19,000
and the hardware got a lot better.

8
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:21,600
Now, here's the thing nobody tells you:

9
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:24,200
the hard part isn't the model.

10
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:26,800
It's everything around it.

11
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,400
How do you keep it
from eating all your memory?

12
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:32,000
How do you make it start fast enough

13
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:34,600
that people don't give up waiting?

14
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:37,200
We tried three different approaches.

15
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:39,800
The first one was a disaster.

16
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,400
Let me show you why.

17
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:45,000
Under the hood, every request

18
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:47,600
loaded the whole model from scratch.
